#
# DEVS:Internet/service_discovery
#
# Servers that run on this Amiga, announced to the rest of the network so that
# a Mac, a Linux box or Windows finds them without being told an address.
#
# This file is not DEVS:Internet/services.  That file is the /etc/services
# table, and it gives the port number that the name "ftp" means, for every
# machine.  This file gives the servers that run on this Amiga, and nothing
# else reads it.
#
# Nothing is announced unless it is listed here.  AmiNetXDuo ships clients and
# no servers, so it has nothing of its own to advertise.  It can advertise a
# separately installed server -- AmiFTPd, a web server, a file server --
# because only the owner of the machine knows that it is running.  Do not
# announce a port with no server behind it.  The other machine lists it,
# connects, and then hangs.
#
# One line per service:
#
#     <type>  <port>  [name]  [txt=key=value;key=value]
#
#   type    what kind of server it is, in the standard form: an underscore,
#           up to fifteen letters, digits or hyphens, then ._tcp or ._udp.
#   port    the port the server listens on, 1 to 65535.
#   name    what it is called in the list on the other machine.  It can
#           contain spaces and runs to the end of the line.  Leave it out to
#           use the host name of this Amiga, which is the usual choice.
#   txt=    extra settings some clients look for, separated by ';'.
#           Optional.
#
# '#' starts a comment anywhere on a line.  A ';' at the start of a line is a
# comment too, but not one in the middle: ';' separates txt= settings.
#
# A line with a mistake in it is reported and skipped.  The rest of the file,
# and the network, come up as usual.
#

# An FTP server on the usual port, listed under this Amiga's own name:
#
#_ftp._tcp     21

# A web server, with a name of its own and the path that browsers open:
#
#_http._tcp    80    Amiga web server    txt=path=/

# Other servers to announce.  Use the port that the server is configured for,
# not the one written here.
#
#_telnet._tcp  23
#_ssh._tcp     22
#_smb._tcp     139   Amiga file share
#_afpovertcp._tcp 548
#_daap._tcp    3689  Amiga music

# At most eight services are announced.
